Subject: [PATCH] Add Supabase Auth login, groups with invite links, and RLS

Task 3 (login):
- Sign-up, sign-in, sign-out and password reset screens using Supabase Auth
  (signUp, signInWithPassword, resetPasswordForEmail, updateUser). The session
  is kept and refreshed by supabase-js and tracked with onAuthStateChange.
- The client sends the access token to Express as a Bearer token. Express
  verifies it with supabase.auth.getClaims() and queries Supabase as that user,
  so row level security applies to every API call.

Task 4 (groups and RLS):
- Record the hosted core schema as a migration so local Supabase and clean
  clones can rebuild it.
- Add invite codes, join_group() and rotate_group_invite(), a trigger that makes
  a group's creator its admin, tighter table grants, and RLS policies on all
  six tables.
- Express routes and React screens to create, join, view and leave groups.
- Attack tests that call the Supabase API directly as an outsider and as a
  member, plus Express token checks (npm run test:rls).
- A benchmark of RLS cost against hand-written membership checks at three
  data sizes (npm run bench:rls).

